From: liujixings <liujixings@outlook.com>
Subject: [PATCH] net: airoha: complete PPE offload for PON, QinQ, multicast and aging

Improve the AN7581 PPE offload paths:

- PON: classify the flow using the outer VLAN tag and the P-bit the PPE
  actually emits (0). Fall back to the "all P-bits share one GEM" check so
  valid VID mappings are no longer rejected.
- QinQ: allow a second VLAN_PUSH and PPPoE_PUSH at the same time, accept
  S-tags (0x88a8) and reject only TPIDs the PPE cannot reproduce.
- VPM: it selects the outer TPID index (1 -> 0x8100, 2 -> 0x88a8), not the
  number of VLAN tags.
- Multicast: read and update native L2B entries through their own layout
  and match the VLAN reported by IGMP snooping.
- Aging: enable the PPE aging bits, scan mode, bind limits and unbind age,
  and expose the bind rate as a module parameter.
- Observability: count every flow that never reaches the FOE together with
  the reason, add a debugfs summary and enable CONFIG_NET_AIROHA_FLOW_STATS
  so per-entry packets/bytes counters are populated for IPv4/IPv6 flows.

Signed-off-by: liujixings <liujixings@outlook.com>
